# Tick-mode lockstep regression
#
# Variant of emulator_smoke that opts into deterministic-time lockstep:
# the bridge advances simavr only when klippy's reactor sends an
# `advance T` over its tick socket, and klippy doesn't process timers
# or fds past T until simavr has advanced there. This eliminates the
# host-load timing skew that makes the parallel sim_time path flaky on
# CPU-contended hosts. We reuse emulator_smoke.cfg unchanged - the
# only difference is the fixture's `tick_mode: true` flag.
#
# This works end-to-end (5/5 on a clean host) after three simavr-tick
# fixes that all had to land together:
#   1. The bridge advances to the first cycle STRICTLY past the requested
#      sim-time (+1) - truncating target*freq stopped the AVR a fraction
#      of a cycle below a reactor.pause() wakeup, so the greenlet never
#      fired and tick livelocked.
#   2. A single-threaded synchronous host-link UART (simavr_bridge.c
#      suart_*) replaces uart_pty's real-time pump thread in tick mode, so
#      bytes move deterministically with each advance (no pump-vs-avr_run
#      race / RX-FIFO loss).
#   3. SIGPIPE is ignored - klippy closes the fixture control socket after
#      pushing the fixture, and the control thread's later "OK" ack write
#      hit EPIPE and SIGPIPE-killed the whole bridge mid-test, read as a
#      spurious serial EOF on klippy's side.
# REQUIRES_EMULATOR (assertions need real MCU responses); skipped, not
# fileoutput-degraded, when no backend is built.
CONFIG emulator_smoke.cfg
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
EMULATOR emulator_tick_mode.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # assertions depend on real MCU responses;

M114
M105
M105
M105

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
